//@version=6
// WAR FORMATION E95b -- INDEPENDENT REPLICATION OF E95 (THE HOLD CAP REMOVED ENTIRELY, PER
// E94's OWN QUEUE ITEM 3), RUN BY A CONCURRENT SESSION THAT DID NOT KNOW E95 EXISTED.
// See EXPERIMENT-LOG.md's E95 (primary record) and E95b (this run) entries. Renumbered E95b
// on rebase per the E94/E94b precedent -- the first-committed entry keeps the number.
//
// PARENT: pine/e94-e93-long-only.pine (E94: E93's 15m 1h-structure cascade, short leg
// mechanically deleted, full 6-year archive). BYTE-IDENTICAL except ONE change: the
// maxBars=288 ("three days") timeout close-out is DELETED, not widened. Everything else
// -- direction gates, structure tier, coil, velocity trigger, whole-number band, witching
// hour ban, shieldUsd/rr -- is untouched.
//
// WHY THIS IS THE RIGHT NEXT QUESTION (not a new sweep):
// ORACLE-RULES.md's own specification correction states the ALCM exit in full: "No
// protective stop. The position ends at target or at liquidation." It names exactly two
// exit events -- shield and target -- and no third, time-based one. The maxBars hold cap
// is not part of the stated ALCM model; it was carried into this construction as an
// engineering convenience (HARD LESSON 1's "trades timing out" failure mode, guarded
// against). E94 found that 22 of its 43 exits (51.16%) hit that cap rather than resolving
// at the shield or the target, and that those 22 capped trades carry PF 3.074932 while the
// 21 that actually resolved score only PF 1.172450 -- i.e. the majority of this build's
// measured edge runs through a mechanism the ALCM spec does not contain. E94's own queue
// named this the one remaining item worth a credit. This run is the direct test: what does
// the construction look like when it is held, exactly as the source specifies, in every
// trade to target or liquidation with no third exit route.
//
// PRE-RUN AUDIT:
//   R = shieldUsd $2,000 against this window's price range, unchanged from E94 (audited
//     there at 1.7%-3.3%, clears the 0.8% floor, HARD LESSON 3).
//   Stop is risk-defined per the ALCM spec (HARD LESSON 5), unchanged.
//   Long leg only (matches E94; short entry mechanically absent, same as parent).
//   BINDING (E17): ONE variable changed from E94 -- the timeout close-out mechanism is
//     deleted outright, not widened to a larger bar count. No entry gate, no shield/rr
//     value, no structure tier touched.
//   REDUNDANCY (HARD LESSON 18): none introduced -- no new term added, one removed.
//   OCCUPANCY CONFOUND, FLAGGED IN ADVANCE (HARD LESSONS 24/28/29, and this is the
//     central risk of this run): under pyramiding=1, a position that no longer times out
//     stays open until it hits the shield or the target, however long that takes. Every
//     one of E94's 22 previously-capped trades will now run longer, and while they occupy
//     the book NO new entry can be admitted. This is expected to REDUCE total trade count
//     relative to E94's 43, not hold it flat -- an occupancy effect, not a selectivity
//     change, and it must not be read as the gate stack becoming pickier.
//   Latch order unchanged from e58a/E78/E79/E94 (HARD LESSON 8).
//
// REGISTERED PREDICTION (HARD LESSON 17), BEFORE RUNNING:
//   1. Trade count falls from 43 -- occupancy from longer-held positions blocks some later
//      entries that E94's cap would have freed up sooner. Not predicting a specific number;
//      predicting only the direction and flagging that a large drop risks the 30-trade floor
//      (LESSON 12) given E94 already sat at the sample edge.
//   2. The 22 trades E94 force-closed at the cap did not have their sign predetermined: each
//      now runs to whichever of shield/target it reaches first. Because those 22 trades were
//      collectively profitable under the cap (PF 3.07), the base rate favours more of them
//      resolving at the 2R target than at the shield, but this is not guaranteed per-trade --
//      a position sitting on an unrealized gain when capped can still reverse into the
//      shield before it ever reaches target. Net PF direction is NOT predicted with
//      confidence; both an improvement (more trades reach full target) and a decline (some
//      reverse hard before target) are consistent with what E94 showed.
//   3. Whatever the trade count and PF, EVERY exit in this run resolves at exactly +2R (shieldUsd*rr
//      points) or exactly -1R (shieldUsd points) from entry -- this is now the FIRST 15m
//      1h-structure result whose exits are entirely the two events the ALCM spec names, with
//      no third route. That is the fact this run exists to establish, independent of whether
//      PF improves.
//
// RATCHET NOTE: this is a structural exit-model test against E94 (its true single-variable
// parent), not a parameter sweep on E94's current shape -- HARD LESSONS 45/49's sweep
// prohibition (E94's gross edge per trade is -$8.16 since 2024) does not bar it, since
// nothing here is being swept past that finding; the finding itself is being tested for
// whether it survives a more faithful exit model. If trade count drops below 30 the result
// is a DIRECTION per LESSON 12, not a bankable number, and RATCHET v2 clause 3 fails outright
// regardless of PF.
//
// RESULT, VERDICT and KEEP/REJECT are recorded in EXPERIMENT-LOG.md and results/backtests.json
// after this run completes, per the lab's provenance rule (never hand-write a metric).
strategy("War Formation E95 15m 1h-structure LONG-ONLY no-timeout", overlay=true,
     pyramiding=1, process_orders_on_close=true,
     commission_type=strategy.commission.percent, commission_value=0.05,
     initial_capital=10000,
     default_qty_type=strategy.percent_of_equity, default_qty_value=100,
     margin_long=100, margin_short=100)

greenBull = input.int(4,     "Green 1h candles for BULL")
greenBear = input.int(2,     "Green 1h candles at or below for BEAR")
skipOpen  = input.int(60,    "Skip first N minutes of 6h block")
skipClose = input.int(60,    "Skip last N minutes of 6h block")
coilK     = input.float(0.85,"Coil: atrFast < atrSlow * K")
velK      = input.float(0.8, "Velocity: min reclaim as multiple of atrSlow")
midLo     = input.float(400, "Whole-number middles low")
midHi     = input.float(600, "Whole-number middles high")
etOffset  = input.int(-4,    "ET offset from UTC")
witchOn   = input.bool(true, "Ban longs in witching hour 1-4am ET")
shieldUsd = input.float(2000,"THE SHIELD: fixed dollar gap to liquidation")
rr        = input.float(2.0, "Reward:risk")

MS6H = 21600000
MS1H = 3600000

b6  = math.floor(time / MS6H)
b1h = math.floor(time / MS1H)

new6  = b6  != b6[1]
new1h = b1h != b1h[1]

var float h1o     = na
var int   grnCur  = 0
var int   cntCur  = 0
var int   grnPrev = 0
var int   cntPrev = 0

if new6
    grnPrev := grnCur
    cntPrev := cntCur
    grnCur  := 0
    cntCur  := 0

if new1h
    if not na(h1o)
        cntCur := cntCur + 1
        if close[1] > h1o
            grnCur := grnCur + 1
    h1o := open

regimeReady = cntPrev >= 5
bullRegime  = regimeReady and grnPrev >= greenBull
bearRegime  = regimeReady and grnPrev <= greenBear

minsIn    = (time - b6 * MS6H) / 60000
timeGate  = minsIn >= skipOpen and minsIn <= (360 - skipClose)

h1Bull = not na(h1o) and close > h1o
h1Bear = not na(h1o) and close < h1o

var float c1hh = na
var float c1hl = na
var float p1hh = na
var float p1hl = na

if new1h
    p1hh := c1hh
    p1hl := c1hl
    c1hh := high
    c1hl := low
else
    c1hh := na(c1hh) ? high : math.max(c1hh, high)
    c1hl := na(c1hl) ? low  : math.min(c1hl, low)

brokeBelow = not na(p1hl) and c1hl < p1hl
brokeAbove = not na(p1hh) and c1hh > p1hh

atrFast = ta.atr(1)
atrSlow = ta.atr(2)
coiled  = not na(atrSlow) and atrSlow > 0 and atrFast < atrSlow * coilK
coilPrev = coiled[1]
velMin   = na(atrSlow) ? na : atrSlow * velK

sub      = close - math.floor(close / 1000) * 1000
inMiddle = sub >= midLo and sub <= midHi

hUTC     = math.floor(time / MS1H) % 24
hET      = (hUTC + etOffset + 24) % 24
witching = hET >= 1 and hET < 4
longBan  = witchOn and witching

longTrig  = not na(p1hl) and not na(velMin) and ta.crossover(close, p1hl)  and (close - p1hl) >= velMin
shortTrig = not na(p1hh) and not na(velMin) and ta.crossunder(close, p1hh) and (p1hh - close) >= velMin

goLong  = bullRegime and timeGate and h1Bull and brokeBelow and coilPrev and not inMiddle and not longBan and longTrig
goShort = bearRegime and timeGate and h1Bear and brokeAbove and coilPrev and not inMiddle and shortTrig

var float slPx = na
var float tpPx = na

flat = strategy.position_size == 0

if flat and goLong
    strategy.entry("L", strategy.long)
    slPx := close - shieldUsd
    tpPx := close + shieldUsd * rr

// E95: maxBars timeout DELETED outright (was 288 bars / 3 days in E94). Every position
// now runs to strategy.exit's stop or limit only -- the two events the ALCM spec names,
// and no third one. No close_all-on-bar-count block exists in this file.

if strategy.position_size > 0
    strategy.exit("LX", from_entry="L", stop=slPx, limit=tpPx)

if strategy.position_size < 0
    strategy.exit("SX", from_entry="S", stop=slPx, limit=tpPx)

plot(goLong  ? 1 : 0, title="LongSignal")
plot(goShort ? 1 : 0, title="ShortSignal")
